From 96ea4b7557d02e10ac42aad42c10b6a327eb3ab0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rafe Walker <45343084+rafe-walker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:53:51 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 04/17] feat(mcp): format query-retention results as a compact
 table

The backend returns formatted_results for trends and funnels but not
for retention, so query-retention fell back to encoding the raw
payload: a URL-encoded copy of the query in _posthogUrl, the query
itself, and 29 cohorts x 8 cells each carrying a null aggregation value
and a repeated label. On the friction session that was 3,874 tokens,
against 303 for trends and 164 for the funnel.

query-retention (and insight-query on a saved retention insight) now
build the text the model reads in services/mcp, in the same pipe-table
style as the backend's trends output:

    Cohorts: first <target>, returning: <returning>, period: Day, from -28d

    Cohort|Size|Day 1|...|Day 7
    2026-10-13|32|9|3|6|4|6|3|3
    ...
    Retained|813|24.2%|20.8%|...

A period that has not started is left blank instead of 0, one still in
progress is marked `*`, and the Retained line is the share returning
per period over the cohorts that completed it. Aggregation queries show
the aggregated values; a breakdown adds a column. The structured
payload the UI app renders, and output_format "json", are unchanged,
and a backend formatted_results still wins when there is one.

On the friction session's retention query this is 759 tokens instead
of 3,874.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
